Z||000005||mshill||01-09-2000||05:14 AM||||OK, so I am ready to drop my cradle, but I am  concerned that the firewall exhaust manifold will not clear the AC compresseor (which I have removed and pushed towards the firewall and passenger side as far as it will go.<P>Can you really get a V6 out without disconnecting the AC hoses?<P>btw,  I am using the two floorjacks and 4x4 just in front of the cradle to get the back into the air.||||reg||5
Z||000006||fiero56||01-09-2000||01:36 PM||||Mshill, are you planning to "hinge" the cradle down, or drop the entire engine/cradle assembly?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mshill||01-10-2000||12:02 AM||||fiero56, it's all coming out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||dogtired||01-10-2000||06:25 AM||||Sounds like you have a good start!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Yes the AC compressor can stay hooked up. Been there done that. Took the two bolts out of the top of the compressor and hung it from the deck lid hinge with a long piece of wire.<BR>I removed the rear wheels and lowered car and cradle down to a furniture dolley, then using the 4X4 under the jack points lifted body up off cradle. Now I removed, plenum, valve cvrs, distributor dogbone and mount and the alternator first. Then I didn't have to jack it up so high and I was able to roll the cradle with motor out the right wheel well??<BR>Make sure you have front wheels BLOCKED real good!<BR>Just some thoughts!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Have Fun!  BE SAFE!||||reg||1
